Third-party data in this repository

- Enron spreadsheet corpus (figshare 1221767), CC BY 4.0: workbooks under benchmarks/external/*/sources/ with names
  starting "enron__". File names contain the original corpus names of the workbook authors.
- UK Open Government Licence v3.0: files starting "ogl" in tests/real/ and benchmarks/external/.
- US federal government works (BEA, IRS, Census), public domain: tests/real/.
- World Bank Open Data, CC BY 4.0 (The World Bank, indicator NY.GDP.MKTP.CD): tests/real/worldbank_gdp.xlsx.
- Each file's source URL, licence and SHA-256 is in the manifest.json next to it.

Data not redistributed here

- Damodaran (NYU Stern) workbooks carry no explicit licence. They are not in this repository.
  `python3 benchmarks/external/realworld2.py fetch` downloads them from the publisher's site and checks them against
  the frozen SHA-256. The benchmark questions and the model answers about them are included.
- SpreadsheetBench (CC BY-SA 4.0) workbooks and raw model responses are not included. `benchmarks/external/spreadsheetbench.py`
  downloads the pinned revision. Only manifests, aggregates and checksums are committed.

Files under tests/real/ and benchmarks/external/ are third-party data. Treat them as untrusted input.
